    /// Fetches a single transaction's detail by id.
    ///
    /// Requires at least `User` in the organization that owns the charging
    /// station the transaction ran on, resolved from the transaction's
    /// connector — plus an explicit environment grant if the caller's role is
    /// exactly `User` (`Owner`/`Admin` reach every environment in their
    /// organization implicitly). A transaction belonging to an environment the
    /// caller cannot access answers `404`, identically to an unknown id, so a
    /// caller cannot distinguish "this transaction does not exist" from "you
    /// cannot see it."
    ///
    /// - Remark: HTTP `GET /v1/transactions/{transactionId}`.
    /// - Remark: Generated from `#/paths//v1/transactions/{transactionId}/get(get_transaction)`.
    func getTransaction(_ input: Operations.GetTransaction.Input) async throws -> Operations.GetTransaction.Output
    /// Computes this transaction's cost fresh from its current usage.
    ///
    /// Nothing is persisted: a running transaction's cost can change between
    /// two reads a second apart if its tariff assignment changes, and even an
    /// ended transaction's cost is recomputed against whatever tariff
    /// resolves now, not whatever applied when the session actually ended. A
    /// caller should treat this figure as "this transaction's cost under
    /// today's pricing," not as an immutable receipt. `noTariffAssigned` means
    /// no tariff resolves for this transaction's scope — the ordinary answer
    /// for most transactions today — and `usageUnavailable` means this
    /// transaction's energy usage is not yet known; neither is the same thing
    /// as a computed cost of `0`.
    ///
    /// - Remark: HTTP `GET /v1/transactions/{transactionId}/cost`.
    /// - Remark: Generated from `#/paths//v1/transactions/{transactionId}/cost/get(get_transaction_cost)`.
    func getTransactionCost(_ input: Operations.GetTransactionCost.Input) async throws -> Operations.GetTransactionCost.Output
    /// Reads a session's charge-by deadline.
