    /// What one session's electricity cost the site
    ///
    /// This is the site's cost of the energy, not what a driver was charged: for
    /// that, see `GET /transactions/{transactionId}/cost`. It is priced when
    /// asked, at the contract in force now and the spot prices published for the
    /// slots the energy was drawn in (`priceBasis: currentContract`), so a figure
    /// can change between two reads and is not an invoice. A session that has not
    /// ended is priced for the energy so far (`running: true`).
    ///
    /// Exactly one outcome. Only `computed` carries an `amount`; every other
    /// outcome is a reason there is none and is never a cost of `0`:
    /// `noSupplyContract`, `usageUnavailable` (fewer than two meter readings),
    /// `pricesUnavailable` (energy was drawn in a slot with no published price;
    /// `unpricedFrom` says where), `currencyMismatch` and `zoneUnknown`.
