    /// `Started`/`Updated`/`Ended` (from the station), plus CSMS-originated
    /// types for a charging-state change, a limit request, and a reported
    /// cost. Cursor-paginated — a typical session's whole log fits on the
    /// default page, so most callers see no difference from an unpaginated
    /// read. Pass `consistencyToken` (see `ListTransactionEventsQuery`) to
    /// wait briefly for this read to catch up to a prior write before
    /// answering; the wait happens before pagination, so a response flagged
    /// `x-consistency-stale: true` still paginates over whatever it actually
